# Git

**Rule Rev.1** — 2026-09-13 (common)

- Conventional Commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `refactor:`, `test:`, `chore:`
- Commit only when the user asks
- Do not commit personal runtime config, slot books, secrets, or `private_*`
- Do not edit a live install’s settings when changing the program; measure in
  an isolated folder
- Author-only Cursor files stay gitignored (`.cursor/rules/private_*`)
